      "writtenOn": "2021-08-05T17:06:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I think what has happened here is that we have a bunch of userfaultfs backports in Android (such as 4a5cf92412ab (\"BACKPORT: FROMGIT: userfaultfd: add UFFDIO_CONTINUE ioctl\")) which mean that pcc\u0027s untagging fix which came in via the upstream stable merges _applies_ cleanly, but breaks the build because it misses the backported cases.\n\nSo I think it\u0027s worth calling out that 0b591c020d28 (\"userfaultfd: do not untag user pointers\") broke the build because of the backport in 4a5cf92412ab (\"BACKPORT: FROMGIT: userfaultfd: add UFFDIO_CONTINUE ioctl\").\n\nI\u0027ve added pcc@ to cc.",
      "parentUuid": "afa80c93_5aa802fb",
      "revId": "438e93fd4ae271ec2211cde655108bcdba089990",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7c04c653_bac3635c",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 8,
